Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Stage 3 scenarios: rejection helper, forged-state option,
 fee TTL; results

- csl_common: fee intents carry a ten-minute TTL (the harness advances
  block time per applied block, and a retained transaction must outlive
  the administrator's update to be tested); TransferOptions gains
  whitelist_override and claim_forged_root; gate_call can run the program
  against a forged copy of the contract state; Rejection, attempt and
  apply_rejected assert on the ledger's disposal of a transaction rather
  than on a prover error, since create_proof emits a proof for any
  witness.
- csl_regulated_transfer: the stale case of T02 asserts the root
  ReadMismatch at replay; T04, T13b and T24 assert InvalidProof; T13a
  (forged root claimed, program run against a forged state) asserts the
  replay failure.
- csl_baseline: exact DUST fee payment with the pay-prove-measure loop.
- docs: results log with the baseline rerun (3 passed) and the nine
  Stage 3 scenarios (9 passed, 236 s) with their disposals; next-steps
  handoff with the findings.

